    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI often want to toggle/invert comments in two lines of code, e.g., convert this:\r\n```\r\n// threshold = 10\r\nthreshold = 100\r\n``` \r\nto this:\r\n```\r\nthreshold = 10\r\n// threshold = 100\r\n```\r\n\r\nPreviously, I used to do this with nerdcommenter by selecting both lines and using `NERDCommenterInvert`.\r\n\r\nI am not sure, but I think this missing feature is referred to in the help file as \"Block and sub-line comments.\r\nI would love to see this feature also for mini.comment - or is it already possible to do this?",
