        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\n> one workaround for visual mode would be using `'<,'>normal gcc<CR>` as suggested here: [numToStr/Comment.nvim#17 (comment)](https://github.com/numToStr/Comment.nvim/issues/17#issuecomment-939410954)\r\n\r\nYes, this was something along the line I was going to suggest using. You possibly might also want to use `config.options.ignore_blank_line = true` to allow this action over blank lines.\r\n\r\nI'll think about if it can be added naturally to 'mini.comment', but at the moment I think the `'<,'>normal gcc<CR>` is the way to go.",
