        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Using `'<,'>normal gcc<CR>` in mapping like `vim.keymap.set('x', 'gi', ':normal gcc<CR>')` does seem like the best approach here. It is not perfect with default options (like blank lines will be commented), but it seems to do a decent job.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can't see how this can organically fit into current design. It will be either a virtually reimplementation of `normal gcc` in a not very optimized way or a complete rewrite of 'mini.comment'. Mostly because current design (for speed reasons) pre-computes action function (whether comment with certain indent or uncomment) and applies it to the whole region.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
